missile-defense (0.9.2-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Starting what is already open now brings its window to the front instead
    of opening it again. The game's TRAIN AI entry used to add another
    trainer with every press, the trainer's Play button refused with a
    message box explaining that it could not raise the game, and a
    double-clicked game icon made a second game. Each program now notices a
    twin showing the same thing, hands it the click and leaves; if nothing
    is running, it starts as before.
  * The same courtesy per replay, model and match: opening the one you
    already have on screen raises that window rather than duplicating it.
    Opening *different* ones still opens windows side by side — comparing
    two recordings on purpose keeps working.
  * MD_SINGLE_INSTANCE=0 turns all of this off, for anyone who genuinely
    wants two of the same window.
  * Trainer, Windows: the Play button could open nothing at all, or a box
    about a Qt platform plugin that could not be initialized. The trainer's
    own toolkit quietly prepends its private copy of Qt to PATH, and the
    game it launched loaded those DLLs instead of the ones it was built
    with. The game now starts with the PATH the trainer was started with —
    and a game run out of a build tree additionally gets the Qt kit its own
    build cache names, so it starts from any shell.
  * Trainer: the Start-a-run dialog no longer opens taller than the display.
    It caps itself to the screen and its tab pages scroll when — and only
    when — the screen cannot hold them; on a display tall enough nothing
    changes.
  * Trainer: the console now fits a 1280-point-wide display. Its minimum
    width was over 2300 points — a sum of one-row headers, seven-button rows
    and labels that refused to wrap — so on small screens a third of the
    window sat past the screen edge. The header and the action rows are two
    rows now, long labels wrap, and as a last resort the whole view scrolls
    rather than the window overflowing the desktop.
  * Trainer: on a machine whose GPU cannot report its memory — a CPU-only
    torch, an AMD card — the memory estimate now draws its bar against
    system RAM and says so; with nothing to measure at all the bar steps
    aside rather than drawing against a made-up total.

 -- Jens Köhler <jens@koehler-speyer.de>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 13:58:27 +0200

missile-defense (0.9.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Windows installer: the Start-menu shortcut pointed at
    bin\missile-defense.exe, one directory below where the game actually
    lands — an entry with no icon that opened nothing, and a finish page
    whose "run Missile Defense" box failed the same way. CPack's NSIS
    generator assumes executables live in bin/ unless told otherwise; it is
    now told.
  * Windows: starting the installed game flashed a console window for every
    Python interpreter probed before the game window appeared. The probe ran
    through _popen, which cannot ask for CREATE_NO_WINDOW; it now spawns the
    interpreter directly, windowless. Only an installed build probes (a
    checkout ships no wheel), which is why no developer ever saw it.
  * Windows: ENTER on "THE TRAINER IS NOT INSTALLED" visibly did nothing.
    The install terminal was spawned through QProcess, which opens console
    children of a GUI process with no window and escapes quotes in a way
    cmd.exe does not read — an invisible cmd holding a mangled command,
    once per keypress. It now gets its own console window and a verbatim
    command line.
  * The TRAIN AI notice for an out-of-date trainer said "PRESS ENTER TO
    UPDATE IT" but opened the instructions page instead. ENTER now runs the
    update it promised.
  * CI: the check that the trainer wheel was staged beside the game guarded
    on an environment variable no step ever set, so it had never run. It is
    unconditional now on both installer legs (Windows and macOS).
  * TRAIN AI now notices a finished install without restarting the game.
    The machine was probed once at startup, so the menu kept answering
    "not installed" after the terminal it had spawned itself said
    otherwise. Anything short of a ready trainer is re-probed each time
    TRAIN AI is chosen — which also notices updates and a Python installed
    mid-session.
  * Windows: the install terminal now opens in front of the game and at a
    fixed 100x30 size. It used to open behind the window that spawned it,
    at whatever size the user's console defaults said — bigger than the
    screen, on the machine that reported it.
  * OPTIONS: the AI SKILL row is gone. It chose the scripted rung WATCH AI
    ran, a decision the WATCH AI submenu has since taken over by naming
    all three rungs itself; the row set something nothing read.

 -- Jens Köhler <jens@koehler-speyer.de>  Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:29:03 +0200

missile-defense (0.9.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * Numbered 0.9.0 rather than 1.0.0 because the macOS build is untested:
    it compiles and its tests pass, but nobody has yet run it on a Mac.

